          "choices": [
            "Type erasure: T does not exist at runtime, and arrays need a reifiable component type \u2014 use ArrayList<T> or Object[] with casts",
            "Arrays of generics are allowed since Java 10 \u2014 upgrade the JDK",
            "T[] requires T to be final \u2014 bound it as <T extends Final>",
            "The syntax is new T[](16) \u2014 the brackets are misplaced"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "why": "Generics are erased at compile time: at runtime a Cache<String> is just Cache, so the JVM could not enforce new T[]'s type safety (arrays are covariant and reified, generics are invariant and erased \u2014 the combination is unsound). ArrayList<T> is the idiomatic replacement; internally it uses Object[] with checked casts.",
          "hint": "What does T become after compilation \u2014 and what does an array need to know at runtime?",
          "objectives": [
