          "answer": 0,
          "why": "computeIfAbsent performs the check-and-compute as one atomic operation (on ConcurrentHashMap, properly synchronized): if the key is absent, the mapping function runs and its result is installed \u2014 no window for a second thread to duplicate the load. The get/put pair has a check-then-act race even on concurrent maps.",
